Stop complement-crypto's Rust RPC server from panicking when the
matrix-rust-sdk returns one of the newer NotificationStatus variants.

matrix-rust-sdk's NotificationStatus enum has grown EventNotFound /
EventFilteredOut / EventRedacted alongside the original Event variant
(notification.rs: `Event { item }`, `EventNotFound`, `EventFilteredOut`,
`EventRedacted`). complement-crypto's GetNotification wrapper only handled
Event and called log.Panicf for everything else. A panic in the RPC server
kills the shared RPC process, so every later test in the same `go test`
process then fails with "connection is shut down" noise, obscuring the
real failures.

Map the non-Event variants to a plain error (which surfaces the actual
variant via %T) so the test fails cleanly and the RPC server stays up.
Note the original panic also printed `%T` of the nil `notifItem` (always
`*matrix_sdk_ffi.NotificationItem`), hiding the true status type; log the
status value instead.

--- a/internal/api/rust/rust.go
+++ b/internal/api/rust/rust.go
@@ -181,9 +181,16 @@ func (c *RustClient) GetNotification(t ct.TestLike, roomID, eventID string) (*ap
 	switch notifItemType := notifStatus.(type) {
 	case matrix_sdk_ffi.NotificationStatusEvent:
 		notifItem = &notifItemType.Item
+	default:
+		// matrix-rust-sdk's NotificationStatus has gained EventNotFound /
+		// EventFilteredOut / EventRedacted variants. The RPC server must not
+		// panic on them: a panic kills the shared RPC process, which cascades
+		// into unrelated tests in the same run ("connection is shut down").
+		// Surface the actual variant (via %T) as a test error instead.
+		return nil, fmt.Errorf("GetNotification: unexpected notification status type %T", notifStatus)
 	}
 	if notifItem == nil {
-		log.Panicf("GetNotification: unexpected notification status type %T", notifItem)
+		return nil, fmt.Errorf("GetNotification: unexpected notification status type %T", notifStatus)
 	}
 	notifEvent := notifItem.Event.(matrix_sdk_ffi.NotificationEventTimeline)
